  "evidence_level": {
    "justification": "The campaign is one accepted, preregistered, single-execution numerical campaign about a declared component model: the accepted L0 conservation model (cft_revival.physics, L0-conservation-reduced-performance) evaluated over a discrete catalogue of the 96 screened sweep designs under the declared multiplicative cusp-survival closure CL-1, whose per-cusp factors are the per-cell collisionless test-particle wall-hit posteriors of the screening dataset (classification SCREENING_L1A_FIELD_TEST_PARTICLE_WALL_LOSS). That is exactly the object the numerical-campaign gate kind was defined for (one accepted campaign on a declared component model), so the kind is reused with its own typed manifest, evidence file, macro-only section, claim records and campaign checker. Its estimands are properties of the optimisers on the mixed categorical-continuous design space (hypervolume per budget, Pareto-set size, seed variance, paired comparisons, which catalogue designs the optimisers select) and of the declared evaluation chain (robust-versus-nominal fronts, the campaign closure versus the pooled-probability sensitivity closure, sensitivity to the binomial uncertainty width). It is optimiser evidence, not performance evidence: it makes no thruster-performance, plasma or physical-device claim, its geometry dependence is the declared identification of a screening wall-hit probability with a per-cusp survival factor and not a validated geometry-to-performance map, it is not the L1 field-resolved reduction (no field solve, no L0 mapping), not L2 and not L3, and it therefore opens none of GATE-L1, GATE-L2 or GATE-L3.",
    "name": "numerical-campaign",
    "opens_gate": null,
    "relation_to_levels": {
      "F0-F3": "an F0-only (corrected analytical) campaign; spec/optimization/campaign-v1.json#benchmark.results stays null",
      "L0": "consumes the accepted L0 model through its Python reference backend; every objective is a ledgered L0 output under the declared closure CL-1 with per-design screening posteriors",
      "L1": "no field solve inside the campaign; geometry enters only as the categorical index of a screened design whose sealed geometry and counts come from the accepted screening dataset on linear-vacuum fields; no geometry-to-L0 map beyond the declared closure",
      "L2": "not coupled to any plasma model; the corrected four-cell solver has no admissible root for interior cusp probabilities and is not used",
      "L3": "not particle-in-cell and not experimental"
    },
    "validation_status": "none: no measurement, facility, or hardware comparison exists",
    "verification_tier": "solution verification of the declared evaluation chain (bit-exact replay of every evaluation, L0 domain integrity, exact hypervolume, monotone curves up to a declared roundoff tolerance, Pareto replay, frozen sample and catalogue hashes, code contract, import-scope equality, duplicate elimination, label consistency) and a predeclared per-design separability check on the campaign and dense records; every binding gate is a recording-integrity gate and acceptance is not an efficacy verdict"
  },
